{{/*
  v2: v1 plus the QRZ postal address and the address rule (LABELS.md rules
  5 and 6). Uses the current LABELS.md through {{.Rules}}; the prompt ID
  hashes the rules too, so an edit there yields a new ID.
*/}}
{{define "system" -}}
You help a radio amateur decide how to send paper QSL cards. A QSL card is a postcard confirming a radio contact.

{{.Rules}}
Answer with one JSON object and nothing else:
{"evidence": "<the words from the record that decided it, quoted exactly and briefly, or empty>", "label": "<{{range $i, $l := .Labels}}{{if $i}}|{{end}}{{$l}}{{end}}>", "via": "<callsign or empty>", "confidence": "<high|medium|low>"}
{{- end}}

{{define "user" -}}
Station: {{.Call}}
Country: {{or .Country "(not stated)"}}

QRZ fields:
qslmgr: {{or .QSLMgr "(empty)"}}
mqsl: {{or .MQSL "(empty)"}}
eqsl: {{or .EQSL "(empty)"}}
lotw: {{or .LoTW "(empty)"}}

QRZ postal address:
{{- if or .Addr1 .Addr2 .State .Zip}}
street: {{or .Addr1 "(empty)"}}
city: {{or .Addr2 "(empty)"}}
state: {{or .State "(empty)"}}
zip: {{or .Zip "(empty)"}}
country: {{or .Country "(empty)"}}
{{- else}} (none)
{{- end}}

QRZ bio{{if .Truncated}} (cut, too long){{end}}:
{{or .Bio "(no bio)"}}
{{- end}}
